     "result_text_tail": " of new-customer revenue is needed to hit the target.\n\nThe deck says openly that the CFO's plan produces about $1.6M more ARR on paper, and gives the reasons for accepting that.\n\n**Choices I made without you:**\n- **Mid-market at 10%, not 12%.** 10% is the only level Palisade has tested. The deck includes moving second-half renewals to 12% (+$0.35M) if early renewals hold up.\n- **Which enterprise renewals are capped:** I assumed capped contracts make up the same 60% share of the enterprise ARR renewing in 2027. The full range is $0.67\u20131.15M.\n- **How strongly SMB customers leave after a price rise:** I scaled the 2023 increase's effect up from 8% to 12%, and doubled it for the bad case because of Inkwell, the cheaper competitor.\n- **Starting point:** I assumed each segment's retention rate over the past 12 months repeats in 2027. \"Growth\" means ARR at the end of 2027.\n- **Proposed thresholds:** the decision triggers on slide 13 and the activation targets are my proposals for leadership to confirm. The pack gives only today's values.\n\n**Not in the pack, but needed before the board meeting:**\n- the 2027 plan for revenue from new customers;\n- the notice periods for renewals (each month of renewals missed costs about $0.36M).\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- `Palisade_2027_Pricing_Decision.pptx`\n- `Palisade_2027_Pricing_Decision_preview.pdf` (my approximate drawing of the slides, not a PowerPoint export)\n\nThe scripts that build the deck and calculate the numbers are in `./build/`."
    }
